            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for slackness, then the Gujarati for to get better."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: દશા",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દશા — daśā — \"a plight; a state of affairs\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો આ વરસે પણ વરસાદ ઓછો પડશે તો ખેતરોની દશા ખરાબ થશે. jo ā varse paṇ varsād ocho paḍśe to khetronī daśā kharāb thaśe. If the rain falls short again this year, the fields will be in a bad way."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દશા (daśā) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit daśā, \"a state, a condition of life\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
